              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3119,
                "end_index": 3206,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This is why unexplained high levels should always be evaluated by a healthcare provider"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3209,
                "end_index": 3547,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### Summary\nIf you are taking a standard daily multivitamin or a low-dose B12 supplement, you do not need to worry about getting \"too much.\" However, if you are taking high-dose supplements (like 1,000+ mcg) or receiving frequent B12 injections without a medical diagnosis of deficiency, it is highly recommended to speak with a physician"
